MODEL_FEEDBACK_JSON:
{
  "positive_alignment_reasons": [
    "Partners and To Be Loved feel like natural next choices because polished vocals and familiar standards connect with what I enjoy in Stages and my vocal crossover listening.",
    "That's Christmas To Me connects with my Christmas listening through seasonal songs and vocal harmonies, while Storyteller recognizes my interest in country music, even though neither is my first choice today."
  ],
  "negative_misalignment_reasons": [
    "In The Lonely Hour and 25 offer strong singing, but vocal ability alone does not give me the orchestral arrangements and theatrical feeling I want right now.",
    "1989 and the Eagles compilation pull away from my current desire for calmer listening; Django and Jimmie also needs a stronger connection than simply fitting my occasional country listening."
  ],
  "overgeneralized_signals": [
    "My interest in expressive singers seems to have been stretched into a broad interest in contemporary pop, although I am more drawn to standards and theatrical vocal performances.",
    "My past Christmas and country listening seems to count as a reason to choose those sounds today, even when I would currently put vocal standards ahead of them."
  ],
  "missing_or_underweighted_signals": [
    "My most recent choice of relaxing classical music suggests that a calm mood and orchestral sound deserve more attention in what I hear next.",
    "The connection among my Downton Abbey music, Stages, and crossover vocal albums is the combination of expressive singing and rich accompaniment, rather than singing alone."
  ],
  "summary_diagnosis": "The recommendations partly understood my taste for polished vocals but stretched it too broadly beyond the calm, orchestral and theatrical listening I want today."
}
